 "decision_rule": "Fresh seed 29, 15 tasks per kind (60 total), tool_active vs c3_alone paired on the same task. TOOL_LIVE_SUPPORTED iff (a) net correct wins >= +10 AND two-sided sign test p < .05, (b) wrong_committed(tool_active) <= wrong_committed(c3_alone), (c) tool_wrong == 0 (the recipe never commits a wrong decision), and (d) no kind loses more than 2 tasks net. Second verdict, fixed in advance as well: TOOL_SHOWN_SUPPORTED iff shown_correct(tool_active) vs correct(c3_alone) (what the user sees including the broker's late correction) has net wins >= +10 AND sign test p < .05 AND (c). Dev seed 7 showed the 350M body often keeps its own decision next to the TOOL_RESULT layer, so the first verdict may fail while the second passes; both are reported. Reported, not part of the verdicts: per kind, proposals, executed calls, read failures, guard refusals, values read exactly, turn time.",
